---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Figure from '../components/diagrams/Figure.astro';
import FlowDefs from '../components/diagrams/FlowDefs.astro';
import WriteReach from '../components/diagrams/WriteReach.astro';
import Topology from '../components/diagrams/Topology.astro';
import LoopCycle from '../components/diagrams/LoopCycle.astro';
import PointerDrift from '../components/diagrams/PointerDrift.astro';
import RunFlow from '../components/diagrams/RunFlow.astro';
import Tradeoff from '../components/diagrams/Tradeoff.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';

const w = site.writeup;

const url = new URL(w.slug, Astro.site).href;
const share = [
  { icon: 'twitter', label: 'X', href: `https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=${encodeURIComponent(w.title)}&url=${encodeURIComponent(url)}` },
  { icon: 'linkedin', label: 'LinkedIn', href: `https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=${encodeURIComponent(url)}` },
  { icon: 'telegram', label: 'Telegram', href: `https://t.me/share/url?url=${encodeURIComponent(url)}&text=${encodeURIComponent(w.title)}` },
];

const DETENT = 'https://github.com/kazimVakhobov/detent';
const ADR = `${DETENT}/blob/main/docs/adr/0012-the-queue-and-the-shared-context-may-be-repositories.md`;
---

<BaseLayout
  path={w.slug}
  title={w.title}
  description={w.description}
  ogImage="/og/agents-need-context-not-access.png"
  ogImageAlt={w.ogAlt}
  ogType="article"
  published={w.published}
>
  <FlowDefs />

  <article class="post">
    <header class="post__head">
      <p class="post__kicker">{w.kicker}</p>
      <h1 class="hero__title">{w.title}</h1>

      <p class="post__stand">
        Agentic development keeps pushing teams into monorepos, so that an agent can see the
        service next door. One documentation repository, mounted into every code repository as
        a git submodule, hands it the same context without the same reach.
      </p>

      <p class="post__meta">
        <span>{w.date}</span>
        <span class="post__sep">·</span>
        <span>{w.readingTime}</span>
        <span class="post__sep">·</span>
        <span>{site.sidebar.name}</span>
      </p>

      <div class="share">
        {
          share.map((item) => (
            <a class="share__btn" href={item.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label={`Share on ${item.label}`}>
              <Icon name={item.icon} />
            </a>
          ))
        }
        <button class="share__copy" type="button" data-copy={url} data-copied-label={site.contact.copied}>
          Copy link
        </button>
      </div>
    </header>

    <h2>The trade a monorepo makes</h2>

    <p>
      An agent reads what is on disk. Put four surfaces in one working copy and it finally has
      the context — and write access to all four.
    </p>

    <p>
      So when the screen fails because the endpoint returns the wrong shape, changing the
      endpoint is the shortest path to green. It will take it. Same incentive that gets a failing
      test edited instead of the code, with a wider radius.
    </p>

    <Figure label="Figure 1" scroll>
      <WriteReach />
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        Both rows give the agent the whole product. Only one of them also gives it the whole
        product to write to.
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>

    <p class="pull">I want the context. I do not want the reach.</p>

    <h2>One repository holds the documents</h2>

    <p>
      Every surface keeps its own repository. One more joins them and holds no
      code: <code>shared-docs</code> — specifications, decisions as numbered ADRs, the task
      queue, a progress log per surface, changelogs. It is mounted into each code repository as
      a submodule, at the same path in all of them.
    </p>

    <p>
      A session — a person and an agent together — writes there. A dispatched agent only reads.
    </p>

    <Figure label="Figure 2" scroll>
      <Topology />
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        <strong>The identical path is load-bearing, not tidiness.</strong> <code>shared-docs/adr/0003.md</code>
        names the same file from the API and from the mobile application, so a link written once
        resolves everywhere.
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>

    <h2>The loop</h2>

    <Figure label="Figure 3" scroll>
      <LoopCycle />
    </Figure>

    <p>
      The boundary holds mechanically rather than by instruction. <code>acme-api/</code> is not
      in the working copy: an instruction not to touch something is a request, and an absent
      directory is not. The blast radius of a bad run is one repository — which is also the unit
      you revert, review and grant access to.
    </p>

    <h2>The friction: a pointer is a pin</h2>

    <p>
      A submodule points at one commit and stays there until somebody moves it. That is right for
      the thing submodules were built for — vendoring a library — and backwards
      here: <code>shared-docs</code> is not a dependency of the web client, it is the same
      product written down, and the whole point of it is that it is current.
    </p>

    <Figure label="Figure 4" scroll>
      <PointerDrift />
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        <strong>One push, N stale pointers.</strong> Nobody did anything wrong in any of those
        four repositories — that is the problem. No diff to review, no check that fails.
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>

    <p>
      So after every write to the documents: <code>git submodule update --remote</code> in each
      repository, then commit the moved pointer. I did that by hand for months, across four
      repositories and then seven. Skip it once and an agent builds against Tuesday's
      specification — correctly, and it passes every check you have.
    </p>

    <p>
      Doing half of it is worse. The update without the commit leaves the superproject
      reporting <code>M shared-docs</code>: a dirty tree holding nobody's work, which every
      check that refuses to run in one now refuses.
    </p>

    <h2>What detent automates</h2>

    <p>
      <a href={DETENT}>detent</a> runs coding agents against a queue of tasks and lets nothing
      finish until the repository's own checks pass. Four moments in a run belong to the
      submodules; between them it does not touch them at all.
    </p>

    <Figure label="Figure 5" scroll>
      <RunFlow />
      <Fragment slot="caption">
        A submodule you want none of this for goes in <code>neverCommit</code>: then it is not
        fetched, not moved and not committed, and the agent is told to leave it alone.
      </Fragment>
    </Figure>

    <p>
      Two of the four I would not have got right by hand. <strong>The commit records what was
      read</strong> — the moved pointer goes into the task's own commit, so the history answers
      "which revision was this built against" instead of somebody's memory. <strong>And it is
      verified before it is recorded</strong> — a commit claiming the agent read revision X when
      it read Y is worse than no record at all, because it looks like one. Written up
      as <a href={ADR}>ADR 0012</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>The trade, line by line</h2>

    <Figure label="Figure 6">
      <Tradeoff />
    </Figure>

    <p>
      None of it is free. The context layer is not generated: if it is not written, there is
      nothing to read and the agent goes back to inferring. And a document is checked by somebody
      reading it, not by a compiler. I would argue for writing the specification first anyway —
      it is still work.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it has run</h2>

    <ul class="bullets post__ran">
      <li><strong>Yuk Markaz 24</strong> — a freight logistics platform: four applications to production in four months, built in parallel over this layer.</li>
      <li><strong>QMed</strong> — a platform for private clinics: seven repositories over one API, one documentation layer, thirty-three ADRs.</li>
      <li><strong>detent</strong> — the tool, open source.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="post__links">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href={DETENT} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <Icon name="github" />
        <span>detent on GitHub</span>
      </a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://detent.kazimvakhobov.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <Icon name="external" />
        <span>detent.kazimvakhobov.com</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="post__back">
      <a href="/">
        <Icon name="arrowLeft" />
        <span>{w.backHome}</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post {
    padding-top: 8px;
  }

  /* --- шапка --- */

  .post__head {
    padding-bottom: 34px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .post__kicker {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .post__stand {
    margin: 20px 0 0;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .post__meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px 8px;
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--faint);
  }

  .post__sep {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .share {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .share__btn {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }

  /* :global — иконки приходят из <Icon> со своим scope */
  .share__btn :global(svg) {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
  }

  .share__btn:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .share__copy {
    height: 34px;
    padding: 0 13px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--muted);
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }

  .share__copy:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* --- текст ---
     Селекторы от прямых детей <article>: в шапке лежат свои <p> со своими
     размерами, и правила основного текста не должны до них доставать. */

  .post > h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    margin: 46px 0 16px;
  }

  .post > p {
    margin: 0 0 15px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .post > p strong,
  .post > ul strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .post > p a,
  .post > ul a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Ключевая мысль статьи: вынос в отступ, без кавычек и курсива */
  .post > p.pull {
    margin: 26px 0;
    padding: 2px 0 2px 20px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .post > ul.post__ran {
    gap: 12px;
    font-size: 14.5px;
  }

  .post__links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 26px;
    padding-top: 26px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .post > p.post__back {
    margin: 26px 0 0;
    font-size: 13.5px;
  }

  .post__back a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .post__back a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .post__back :global(svg) {
    width: 15px;
    height: 15px;
    flex: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .post__stand {
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .post > h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
      margin-top: 38px;
    }

    .post > p.pull {
      font-size: 18.5px;
    }
  }
</style>
